# nbli codecpack — NBLI prototype v0.4 (algo 16, INVFS_ALGO_NBLI).
#
# Open-prototype leg of the WP620 two-way photo handler. Default stays jxl;
# nbli is opt-in (`-o photo_codec=nbli` / `INVFS_PHOTO_CODEC=nbli`). The
# engine's PNG lane drives this pack's encode/decode trampolines directly.
# Lane-driven, but NOT sniff-free: one sniff.magic (the PNG signature) is
# claimed so the WP103 try-last loop skips it (that loop only offers
# claim-free packs a trial run, and a trial nbli encode on every binary
# file would fork+exec per file and stamp GENERIC_GUARD{16} over the
# generic floor's verdict). The WP13 claimed loop can therefore only offer
# it PNG-magic files -- which the builtin PNG branch always decides first,
# so in practice only <33-byte PNG-magic garbage ever arrives there.
#
# The stored shape is the PNGR one with the pixel codec swapped: the
# NBLI blob in a "name!nbli" sibling plus the same IVPN recipe (deflate
# replica of the original IDAT).
#
# NBLI is single-image-only (no inter-frame coding): the lane is a per-file
# codec choice, not a series mode. JPEG input is NOT claimed: NBLI has no
# JPEG-bitstream-reconstruction mode (that is the JXL lane's whole trick),
# so on JPEG the photo handler keeps the JXL path whatever the knob says.
#
# Payload: open NBLI prototype sources ONLY (src/NBLI + src/imageio +
# src/FileIO.h + LICENSE + README at upstream commit 6561fc8), built
# static at pack-build time (payload.bin). The closed fNBLI binary is
# disqualified by policy: never downloaded, never staged, never executed.
# The prebuilt NBLI / NBLI.exe / fNBLI / fNBLI.exe files the upstream tree
# ships are stripped from the payload, and src/fNBLI is not vendored.
#
# Payload construction (reproducible):
#   git clone https://github.com/WangXuan95/NBLI && git checkout 6561fc8
#   keep {LICENSE, README.md, src/NBLI, src/imageio, src/FileIO.h},
#   drop everything else (src/fNBLI, prebuilt binaries, image/, .git),
#   find nbli-payload -type f | sort |
#     tar --mtime='2024-09-01' --no-recursion -czf nbli-6561fc8.tar.gz -T -
#
# Build note: src/imageio/uPNG/uPNG.c includes "upng.h" (lowercase) but the
# file is uPNG.h -- an upstream case bug. The build leg links the lowercase
# name to the real header inside the UNPACKED build tree (never in the
# hash-pinned payload), the same class of build-tree-only fix as the
# WP619 mac wide-stdio shim.
#
# NBLI CLI (v0.4): input .png/.ppm/.pgm/.pnm, output .nbli (encode) and the
# reverse (decode). Explicit -o is REQUIRED: a bare positional second arg
# is parsed as another INPUT (verified: `nbli a.png a.nbli` compresses a.png
# to its default name, then tries to decompress a.nbli). -f forces
# overwrite. Only 8-bit RGB and gray round-trip: RGBA drops alpha with a
# warning, 16-bit and interlaced are refused -- the lane's decode-back
# pixel memcmp is what refuses those files, never this argv.
#
# Payload license: GPL-3.0-only (upstream LICENSE). External tool only
# (fork+exec, never linked): no engine license impact.
